#29801
butler~
The butler~
A frail old butler is standing here.~
The butler looks very tired and strangely out of place in this foreboding
house. You wonder for how many years he has been answering the front door.~
ACT_SENTINEL|ACT_SMART|ACT_BODY|ACT_RACE
AFF_DETECT_INVIS|AFF_DETECT_HIDDEN|AFF_SANCTUARY|AFF_UNDERSTAND
1000 S
95 BODY_HEAD|BODY_EYE|BODY_HAND BODY_HAND|BODY_FOOT 4d100+12600 14d14+10
100000 RACE_HUMAN
POS_STANDING POS_STANDING SEX_MALE
>all_greet_prog 100~
sigh 
if quest (0,5,$n) == 0
  tell $n I have been trapped in here for as long as I can remember,
  tell $n forced to do the work of the evil Lelik. Many times have I
  tell $n wished for my freedom, so that I may die in peace,
  tell $n but there seems no hope of escape.
endif
~
>speech_prog escape~
if quest (0,5,$n) != 23
  if quest (6,2,$n) != 2
    mpmadd $n quest 6 2 1
    mpmset $n quest 0 5 1
    say The only way I could ever escape is if I were to possess a certain glowing gem, which has great power.
  else
    mpecho Sorry, the quest is over for you - try again next life!
  endif
else
  say I have already received your aid!
endif
~
>speech_prog gem~
if quest (0,5,$n) == 1
  say I believe that there is a vampire in the house that has it, but I very much doubt he will part with it. He has the power even to take it with him to beyond the grave.
mpmset $n quest 0 5 2
endif
~
>speech_prog grave~
if quest (0,5,$n) == 2
  say Hrmm, it's rumoured that there is a way to persuade the vampire to spare the gem to whoever defeats him, I really don't know.  Perhaps one skilled in the art of persuasion can help you with that.
endif
~
>all_greet_prog 100~
if quest (0,5,$n) == 3
  mpmset $n quest 0 5 4
  say Well done! I did not think that you would be able to convince the vampire to part with the gem. Now, give me the gem so that I may escape.
endif
~
>give_prog I29808~
if quest (0,5,$n) == 4
  mpjunk i29808
  mpmset $n quest 0 5 5
  say Thank you for this valuable gift!
  mpecho The butler examines the gem intently. Then he frowns.
  shout NO! What has he done!
  say The vampire has defiled the holiness of the stone. It will have to be purified now. I have heard of an anti-evil lotion, but I do not how to make one, or where to find any.  I would value it greatly if you could find some for me.
else
  give i29808 $n
  say I don't want this now.
endif
~
>give_prog I29815~
if quest (0,5,$n) == 16
  mpjunk i29815
  mpmset $n quest 0 5 17
  say AMAZING! You found it! Now I can purify the gem.
  mpecho The butler rubs the lotion all over the gem, and it changes into a brilliant pearl colour.
  say I have bad news for you, though. Someone has stolen the bracket that I need to mount the gem in, but I don't know who. Someone in this house must have it on them.  Perhaps you can locate it.  Without it I cannot escape.
  mpquiet on
  mpjunk all
  mppurge
  mpoload 29816
  if rand (25)
    mpmload 29827
    give bracket nightmare
    mpat 29810 mppurge
    mptransfer nightmare 29810
    else
    if rand (33)
      mpmload 29832
      give bracket rotting
      mpat 29874 mppurge
      mptransfer rotting 29874
      else
      if rand (50)
        mpmload 29825
        give bracket astronomer
        mpat 29808 mppurge
        mptransfer astronomer 29808
      else
        mpmload 29834
        give bracket mummy
        mpat 29877 mppurge
        mptransfer mummy 29877
      endif
    endif
  endif
  mpquiet off
else
 give i29815 $n
 say What is this you are giving me?
endif
~
>give_prog I29816~
if quest (0,5,$n) == 17
  mpjunk i29816
  mpmset $n quest 0 5 18
  mpecho The butler takes the gem and mounts it into the bracket.
  mpjunk all
  say Hmmm, now all that is needed is to align it correctly to the stars. I'm afraid I don't quite know how to do that.  Perhaps the astronomer can help you with that.
else
 give i29816 $n
 say I don't need this yet.
endif
~
>speech_prog p align the bracket to the Orion constellation at midnight on the first day of the month of the Old Forces.~
if quest (0,5,$n) == 22
  mpmset $n quest 0 5 23
  say Finally!!! I can be free! Thank you for this great service you have done for me. I shall reward you grandly. Here, take this. It has been in my family for more years than I can think of.
  mpoload 29817
  give heirloom $n
  mpquiet off
  say I would give you the armour that was once mine, but Lelik holds it in a magical void.
endif
~
>speech_prog void lelik armour~
if quest (0,5,$n) == 23
 mpmset $n quest 0 5 24
 Say I have often tried to pull the armour out, but his power is too great for me to do that.  Perhaps you are strong enough to defeat him.
 mpoload 29850
 give i29850 $n
 drop i29850
 say Take this rune and give it to Lelik.  It will allow you to destroy him.
endif
~
>all_greet_prog 100~
if quest (0,5,$n) == 25
  Say Well done! I can't believe that you managed to kill that foul fiend. Here, let me try to retrieve my armour ...
  mpecho The butler closes his eyes, frowns and then smiles. A set of armour appears as if by magic!
  mpquiet on
  cast 'cure blindness'
  mpmset $n quest 0 5 26
  mpquiet off
  mpoload 29823
  mpoload 29824
  mpoload 29825
  mpoload 29827
  mpoload 29828
  mpoload 29830
  mpoload 29831
  drop all
  mpquiet on
  cast 'giant strength' $n
  cast 'bless' $n
  cast 'sanctuary' $n
  cast 'enhanced heal' $n
  cast 'enhanced revive' $n
  cast 'enhanced rest' $n
  cast 'fly' $n
  cast 'stability' $n
  cast 'ethereal travel' $n
  cast 'astral projection' $n
  cast 'shield' $n
  cast 'armor' $n
  cast 'mirror image' $n
  cast 'tongues' $n
  cast 'understand' $n
  cast 'breath water' $n
  cast 'infravision' $n
  cast 'invis' $n
  cast 'change sex' $n
  cast 'refresh' $n
  cast 'refresh' $n
  cast 'refresh' $n
  cast 'feast'
  mpquiet off
  mpecho You feel better!
  smile
endif
~
>fight_prog 100~
if rand(5)
  flip $r
else
  if rand(20)
    cast 'acid blast' $r
  else
    if rand(100)
      cast 'cure critical'
      cast 'cure critical'
    else
    endif
  endif
endif
~
>fight_prog 100~
if isevil ($n)
  say May all evil be purged from the realms!
  cast 'dispel evil' $r
  cast 'dispel evil' $r
  cast 'dispel evil' $r
  cast 'dispel evil' $r
  cast 'dispel evil' $r
endif
~
>fight_prog 50~
disarm $n
~
>fight_prog 10~
martialarts
~
>speech_prog p let me out~
  say Very well. I'm glad you've decided to leave this awful place.
  mpecho The butler walks over to the door and starts to draw back the bolts.
  say Curse these bolts. I never get around to having them oiled.
  mpecho The butler produces a key from nowhere and unlocks the door. Before you know it's gone, the key vanishes, just like that!
  mpecho The butler shows you all out the door.
  say Farewell! And have a safe journey!
mptransfer pcs 29865
mpat 29865 mpecho The butler closes the door behind you. You hear the bolts being driven home and the key turning in the lock.
~
>rand_prog 5~
sigh 
say I'm getting too old to do this for too much longer.
~
>rand_prog 5~
say There is still so much evil in the world.
~
