  mpmset $n quest 0 5 8
  say No.
  look $n
  grumble $n
  say Well, I might consider it if you can help me with something.
endif
~
>speech_prog help~
if quest (0,5,$n) == 8
  mpmset $n quest 0 5 9
  say I was walking through the house and by mistake I walked into the lair of the beasts. In my haste to escape I dropped my magic spoon. If you can get it back for me, I would consider helping you out.
endif
~
>give_prog I29813~
if quest (0,5,$n) == 9
  mpmset $n quest 0 5 10
  mpjunk i29813
  say Thank you! At last my cooking can once again be as good as it should.
  ponder
  say Now, what did you want again $n?
else
  give i29813 $n
  say I don't need this yet.
endif
~
>give_prog I29812~
if quest (0,5,$n) == 11
  mpjunk i29812
  mpmset $n quest 0 5 13
  say Good. Now I will need some fine dust. It has to be very finely ground, though.  I'm sure you can find some laying around somewhere.
else
  say Thanks, I can always use more blood.
  mpjunk i29812
endif
~
>give_prog I29811~
if quest (0,5,$n) == 13
  mpmset $n quest 0 5 14
  mpjunk i29811
  say Well done! Hmmm, let me think now ... Yes. I'll also need a multi-coloured powder.  I know I saw some on the floor somewhere.
else
  say Thanks, I can always use more dust!
  mpjunk i29811
endif
~
>give_prog I29810~
if quest (0,5,$n) == 14
  mpmset $n quest 0 5 15
  say There we go! Now I can go about making the lotion ...
  mpecho The cook pulls a pot out of one of the cupboards and starts to mix the ingredients together.
  mpecho There is a blinding flash of light and you are momentarily blinded.
  mpecho Then you see a multi-hued mixture in the pot.
  say Damn. I can't get the mixture hot enough.  This is the best I can do for you. It's not finished, but if you can perhaps give it to something really really hot to heat it up enough, it will be finished.  There, I owe you nothing anymore. Go away now and let me cook.
  mpoload 29814
  give I29814 $n
  drop i29814
  mpjunk all
else
  mpjunk i29810
  say Thanks!  I can always use more powder!
endif
~
|
