#ROOMS
#29800
The bell tower.~
This room has a magnificent view of the surrounding countryside. There is a
large bell hanging from the roof and the walls are open to the outside. A
walkway runs around the bell on the inside of a small wall, presumably there to
prevent one from falling down out of the tower.~
298 ROOM_NO_MOB|ROOM_SAFE SECT_INN
DDIR_DOWN
The steps lead down.~
~
0 -1 29804
E
bell~
The bell is made out of brass, as bells are prone to be made out of. You
suspect that it was once in use on a daily basis, but now it seems to be more
or less left on its own.~
S
#29801
The attic.~
Dusty would be a rather severe understatement if used to describe this room.
There is dust lying everywhere - on the wooden floor, on the various chests in
the room and also on you. There are a few photographs lying around. You cough.~
298 ROOM_INDOORS SECT_INSIDE
DDIR_SOUTH
The attic continues south.~
~
0 -1 29804
DDIR_DOWN
You see the landing down there.~
~
0 -1 29811
E
chest chests~
The chests are all tightly locked up with large padlocks. They are sturdy and
strong and probably contain a whole host of sickening family memories.~
S
#29802
The top of the cell.~
This part of the cell has a plain wooden bed with dirty linen. There is a
small basin in the one corner and a window in the wall. Though it is not quite
alcatraz, it would not be overly pleasant to spend any amount of time in this
place.~
298 ROOM_INDOORS SECT_INSIDE
DDIR_DOWN
The stairs lead down.~
~
0 -1 29813
E
window~
The view out of the window is the one saving grace of the cell. It truly is one
worth viewing. However, one can only spend so much time staring out a window
without going balmy.~
E
bed~
The bed looks old, cold and uncomfortable. You suspect that there is a
profusion of lice in the bed.~
S
#29803
The attic.~
The attic here is dusty. It has probably been a while since anyone has been
here. There are various family-type things lying around: there is a teddybear
and a doll's pram. You wonder why people bother keeping all their old stuff.~
298 ROOM_INDOORS SECT_INSIDE
DDIR_EAST
The attic continues north.~
~
0 -1 29804
E
pram~
The pram is a toy for a little girl. You wonder where she could be.~
E
bear teddy~
This teddybear probably once made a little child very happy. You doubt, 
however, whether this person is now younger than about eighty. It should be 
donated to a charity organisation.~
S
#29804
The attic.~
The attic is covered with dust. There are various items of nostalgic value
lying around. Somebody has a lot of fond memories lying around here. You wish
that someone would come up here once in a while to clean out all the dust.
There are stairs leading up.~
